   "lisa_shop_intro": "Let's go to the shop! I've got a purse, and there's money in it.",
   "lisa_shop_basket": "Put the things I ask for in the basket.",
   "lisa_shop_price": "Listen to how much it costs.",
   "lisa_shop_pay": "Now let's pay. Move the money over to the till.",
   "lisa_shop_count": "Let's count together!",
   "lisa_shop_more": "It's not quite enough yet. Add a coin.",
   "lisa_shop_extra": "Oops, there's one coin too many. Take one back.",
   "lisa_shop_exact": "Exactly the right amount!",
   "lisa_shop_change": "You gave more, so the shopkeeper gives you change.",
   "lisa_shop_swap": "Look: these little coins are worth the same as one big one.",
   "lisa_shop_note": "And this is paper money. It's called a banknote.",
   "lisa_shop_find": "Find one just like this.",
   "lisa_shop_euro": "This is the euro. People pay with it in Portugal, in Germany and in lots of other countries.",
   "lisa_shop_cent": "The little coins are cents. A hundred cents make one euro!",
   "lisa_shop_finish": "Everything's in the basket! You paid all by yourself, just like a grown-up.",
   "lisa_shop_travel": "Let's fly to another country! They have their own money there.",
   "lisa_cur_gbp": "In England, people pay with pounds and pence.",
   "lisa_cur_usd": "In America, people pay with dollars and cents.",
   "lisa_cur_chf": "In Switzerland, people pay with francs.",
   "lisa_cur_jpy": "In Japan, people pay with yen.",
   "lisa_cur_rub": "In Russia, people pay with roubles and kopecks.",
   "lisa_cur_brl": "In Brazil, people speak Portuguese too! And they pay with reais.",
   "lisa_fact_pt": "In Portugal, people take their own bag to the shop. You can use it again and again!",
   "lisa_fact_uk": "In England, a new bag at the shop costs money. That's why lots of people bring their own.",
   "lisa_fact_us": "In America, the price label often has a little hint: which pack is better value.",
   "lisa_fact_ch": "In some shops in Switzerland, people weigh their own fruit and stick on a little label with the price.",
   "lisa_fact_jp": "In Japan, people often put money on a little tray instead of into someone's hand.",
   "lisa_fact_ru": "In Moscow there are fairs at the weekend. They sell apples and vegetables right out in the street!",
   "lisa_fact_br": "In São Paulo there are street markets called feiras. There's so much fruit there!",
   "lisa_country_choose": "Where shall we fly next time? If you like, tap a picture.",
